// Clue Name :
"P3143336874" "Metal Cages"
// DetailString :
"P1132555945" "This poem is strange, but you have to wonder if the metal cage it refers to means a clockwork. Maybe Alec Parson could help shed some light on this for you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MetronomeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2854913258" "Metronome"
// DetailString :
"P3612064404" "Alec appears to have been a very busy man lately, keeping track of the movements of the Metronome entity, and even piecing together its motives. According to him, Metronome is on a vengeance quest against Praetor Keyes. Alec believes that the Metronome virus was planted by one of the early researchers who worked on the Clockwork with Keyes, a man by the name of Russell Brandt."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WhereaboutsClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3846341258" "Metronome's Whereabouts"
// DetailString :
"P1718802707" "Alec told you that Metronome's clockwork just broke into a tech facility in Neutropolis and the PPD have already responded. He also recommended that you don't get involved."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MetalManClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4136573836" "Metronome, the man in the metal cage"
// DetailString :
"P748248297" "You recited the poem to the clockwork and for a moment its rage subsided.<br><br>Could it be that Metronome isn't a computer virus at all, but rather the man named Russell Brandt trapped inside the clockwork?<br><br>You have a feeling that the only way you are going to find out is by asking the girl who seems to know these raging robots best, Penelope Yin."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1805824574" "A poem stirs in your mind as if it were you own, but also pointedly not."
// SendOffString :
"P1244595619" "There was a boy long ago<br>whose heart was pure as light.<br>But when that boy was met by death<br>his soul remained to fight.<br>Endure he does in metal cages<br>seeking his revenge.<br>Please tell a metal cage of his<br>our love will never end."

